    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 3 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Win money by betting that your hand contains a higher card of the same suit than the dealer's spot card (a six or lower); the dealer banks the pot and pays or collects each bet.",
      "Turn-flow example: Dealer puts up a stake (the pot). Dealer deals three cards face-down to each other player; players must not look at their cards. Dealer then turns cards face up in the centre until a six or lower appears; that card is the spot card. In turn, each player bets an amount between an agreed minimum and the current pot that they hold a higher card of the same suit than the spot card. After the player bets, the player's hand is exposed. If it contains a higher card of the same suit, the player wins that stake from the pot; otherwise the bet is added to the pot. If the pot becomes empty during the hand, the deal passes to the next player who creates a new pot. At the end of the hand, the dealer keeps whatever remains in the pot and the deal passes to the next player.",
